A||||29||artherd||Why the Fiero is an Exotic Sports Car...||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||12-05-2001||03:49 AM||||The engine is aft of the passenger compartment, yet forward of the rear axel. "Mid Engine."<P>It requires a high level of care and upkeep, but will reward you with a unique and high-level of driving expierence not found in ordinary cars.<P>5 gears, 4 wheels, 2 Seats, no cupholders.<P>I think that the Fiero fully qualifies as an Exotic car, with all the ascendant driving ability, and required attention.<P>It just happens to be pretty inexpensive :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Fformula88||12-05-2001||10:13 AM||||Interesting way of looking at it, and I think you may have a good point.  Although I am not sure it should be put up there with Ferrari's and Lamborgini's, just yet.  Originally there may have been a few too many on the roads to to truly be exotic... I consider being fairly raer a component... but as time goes on and there are fewer and fewer on the road, maybe they are becoming more exotic!<P>Or is that extinct?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  j/k!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||12-05-2001||10:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<P><BR>5 gears, 4 wheels, 2 Seats, <B>no cupholders.</B><P><BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL!<BR>Thats descriptive enough  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-05-2001||11:08 AM||||Ill agree with sports car, no doubt. But falls way short of being an exotic. Exotics are usually limited production run. Hundreds of thousands wont qualify in my opinion, no matter how good. Production Corvettes arent exotics for the same reason. Some like Greenwood or Callaway may be though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||12-05-2001||11:30 AM||||I agree with Roger, and would add that a higher degree of refinement/build quality would be in order to meet the modern criteria for "exotic" status. <BR>Many would argue that the Pantera is an exotic, but others would say by my criteria it wouldn't qualify since their quality, particularly their rustproofing, leaves something to be desired.<BR>As much as I love Fieros and working on them, I think I'd be able to enjoy what's so much better about their layout than other cars if some arcane little part wasn't failing as soon as my back is turned. It's as if they have a life of their own!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||12-05-2001||01:13 PM||||Reminds me of the argument a guy used when he took his T-bucket to a British "sports car" show....<P>"It's drafty, rides rough and leaks oil, <I>of course it's a sports car!!!</I>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-05-2001||02:37 PM||||If youve ever driven a T-bucket, youd know its very very very far from being a sports car. There not good at anything other than going in a straight line.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||12-05-2001||03:35 PM||||Going by Roger's qualifications in, maybe there is hope for the Fiero in the form of a Mera.  Very low volume, definately different in appearance anyway.  It could be on the outskirts of exotic.||||reg||1
