Z||000017||artherd||12-06-2001||03:12 AM||||Intresting!! I never even thought of the production volume being an issue, to me a Ferrari would still be a Ferrari even if everybody on the planet had one (and the world would be a much better place!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>But many people don't agree, infact Ferrari purpously limits the production of their cars, but to keep the 'small factory' and handbuilt nature of their cars intact, AND to increase their rarity/demand.<P>Can't blame 'em, even at $140,000 for the engine ALONE, a 360 is a steal.  And then they throw in a whole CAR for free!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fformula88||12-06-2001||10:05 AM||||Hey BS... I think this is thread was about having some fun with the notion of the Fiero being kind of exotic because it is different.  Not a declaration the a 4 cyl Fiero is in the same class of vehicle as a Ferrari.  Your entitled to your opinion of course, but so is everybody else here and IF someone wants to think their car is somewhat exotic, then to them it is and that is what matters.||||reg||1
