Z||000021||artherd||12-06-2001||05:51 PM||||Yep! Well, that's if you take it to V8 archie for his 'required maintinence' :)<P>And just like the other exotics, if you MISS those service invervals, you're totally screwed (think 84s igniting because nobody changed the oil, or let it accumulate where it shouldn't....)  <P>You've got to treat these cars quite exactly like you'd treat a Ferrari or Lotous!<P><BR>PS: I actaully am saying that a 4-cyl 84 needs to be taken care of just like an 84 Lotous 2.2 turbo :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PPS: and yes, that 4-cyl mustang is just like the cobra-R, a chassis with an engine in front, and both a poor shaddow of the 1960s stangs :) &lt;ducks and runs away&gt;<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>  <BR>high up keep eh? so it has $5,000 tune ups too?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
