Z||000029||artherd||12-08-2001||03:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>So if thats what makes an exotic, so is Porsche 914, MR2, </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, yes, but we do have to draw the line at the pickup! (!!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (thought it was FWD?)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>That definition also rules out all front engine Ferraris and Lambos which are definately exotics. Number one issue to be exotic is 'Rare' or unusal.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A fiero in good condition? &lt;ducks and runs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">&gt;<P>I didn't mean to suggest that these criteria were exclusive (eg, that all cars with fewer or more than 5 gears were not exotic.)  but just as a list.<P>I still say that if you treat your Fiero like a Ferrari, it will treat you like one too!<P>Er, it will treat you as though it were a ferrari at least.  Yeah. anyway.  <BR>mid-engine rocks!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
